  56:     """
  57:     Remove blank separator columns and slide each vertical object group so adjacent connector endpoints touch.
  58: 
  59:     Input structure
  60:     A short strip contains monochrome path-like object groups, each occupying a contiguous run of non-background columns; runs are separated by all-background columns. Each group has a unique degree-1 foreground endpoint on both its left and right outer edge.
  61: 
  62:     Rule
  63:     Delete the all-background separator columns. Keep the first group in its original vertical position, then process the remaining groups from left to right: shift each group vertically, without rotation or recoloring, so its left endpoint is on the same row as the previous placed group's right endpoint, and paste it immediately to the right.
  64: 
  65:     Key insight
  66:     The intended contacts are the degree-1 edge endpoints, not every possible foreground edge overlap, which makes the packed strip a single connected chain.
  67:     """
